; A sign before a date is a token of its own, which no directive starts
; with, and the date after it is still a date: beancount reports the sign
; and reads the directive from the date on. So the open on line 6 is kept
; and the one on line 7 is its duplicate; a signed date is no metadata
; value and no cost date either.
-2020-01-01 open Assets:A
2020-01-02 open Assets:A

2020-01-03 open Assets:B
  when: -2020-01-05

2020-01-04 * "a signed cost date"
  Assets:A  1 HOOL {5 USD, -2020-01-05}
  Assets:A
